# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build output
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local data and sessions
.pax-data/
.strands/

# Generated verification/test artifacts. The demo deliverables under
# artifacts/demo/ are submission output, not build output, so they are
# deliberately kept.
#
# `artifacts/*`, not `artifacts/`: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so with a bare `artifacts/` every negation below is dead and the
# allowlisted deliverables cannot be added at all -- which is the opposite of
# what those lines say they do.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/demo/
artifacts/demo/*
!artifacts/demo/sift-webmcp-demo-FINAL.mp4
# The AWS cut is allowlisted under its FINAL name only. The current file is
# sift-aws-energy-demo-DRAFT.mp4 and stays untracked on purpose: its footage is
# real, but its voice track is macOS `say` and the video says DRAFT on its own
# face. Re-voice it (see rec/energy/REVOICE.md), rename it to the name below,
# and it becomes committable without touching this file.
!artifacts/demo/sift-aws-energy-demo-FINAL.mp4
# The Agents for Humans hero changed to bid-comparison on 2026-09-07
# (docs/decisions/0017-bid-comparison-professional-agents-hero.md). No video
# has been recorded for it yet, draft or final -- this allowlists the FINAL
# name in advance, following the same <track>-<hero>-demo-<STATUS>.mp4
# convention as the two entries above, so the recorded cut can actually be
# committed once it exists. Record from
# docs/submissions/agents-for-humans/demo-script-bid.md.
!artifacts/demo/sift-aws-bid-demo-FINAL.mp4
!artifacts/demo/screenshots/
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.playwright-mcp/
.stryker-tmp/
reports/mutation/

